{{Navbar modding}}
<translate>
<!--T:1-->
'''Rendering''' is the process of generating a 2D image from a 3D model by means of a 3D software. [[Wikipedia:Blender|Blender]] is one of the most popular in the Project Zomboid community, but there are many others available. Rendering is indirectly linked to {{ll|modding}}, as it is mostly used to create images to be used in your mod presentation, or inside various medias in-game such as {{ll|flier}}s in {{ll|Build 42}}.

<!--T:2-->
The process usually involves getting the game assets in the 3D software, which is decently covered in {{ll|File formats#Importing assets}}, but some game assets like tiles are only 2D sprites without actual 3D models. This involves a different process, where you recreate the 3D model shape and adjust the UV map to fit the 2D texture.

== Getting started == <!--T:7-->
A serie of video guides have been made by [https://www.youtube.com/@sqzpz SQz] and are often used as a reference for learning how to render Project Zomboid in [[wikipedia:Blender|Blender]], however it has now became a bit outdated. The [[Community rig]] provides an easy to use tool in Blender for managing and dressing up a character, setting its body texture, model, hair etc. The [[Online Asset Library]] also provides different tiles made as 3D assets directly usable in Blender. When it comes to retrieving every clothing of the game, if you don't plan on using the Community rig which does it for you, you can learn how to import the assets in [[Importing assets]].

A better in-depth guide on how to use those tools was made in the [[Sit-Down Sunday]] of the 4th of October, 2026, presented by the creator of the [[Community rig]] and [[Online Asset Library]], Paddlefruit.

